{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-122463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/assets/e3614ea1954f36435eb1ab5f52c04d4fa3062ac337eccf76a5b47e4a03a64a1b.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/state.json" "file_sha256" "2aaa69da7f902eacd1701b38c030cc87f3707a2961bdb9493a5cd1afb18e6c70"} {"question" "q-122463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We notice the following:\n\n- The horizontal component (i.e., the $i$ component) is negative for each vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following options:\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=i-2\\,j,\\,H(x,y)=i\n$$\n\n- The vertical component (i.e., the $j$ component) is positive for each vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nK(x,y)=-j\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $G(x,y)=-i+j.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/state.json" "file_sha256" "2aaa69da7f902eacd1701b38c030cc87f3707a2961bdb9493a5cd1afb18e6c70"} {"question" "q-122463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5c3df36c5a5a48ba44e555bfdebc8a7077212df2cdc73b3578a5a527e6f046f7"} {"question" "q-122463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/state.json" "file_sha256" "2aaa69da7f902eacd1701b38c030cc87f3707a2961bdb9493a5cd1afb18e6c70"} {"question" "q-122463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "F(x,y)=i-2\\,j"] ["math" "G(x,y)=-i+j"] ["math" "H(x,y)=i"] ["math" "K(x,y)=-j"] ["text" "None of the listed"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/state.json" "file_sha256" "2aaa69da7f902eacd1701b38c030cc87f3707a2961bdb9493a5cd1afb18e6c70"} {"question" "q-122463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "G(x,y)=-i+j"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/state.json" "file_sha256" "2aaa69da7f902eacd1701b38c030cc87f3707a2961bdb9493a5cd1afb18e6c70"} {"question" "q-122633" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/assets/251e49513353092b4f9a16f54bb14fbaa1afe1a14e5fecf5b3ce54905fed474d.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/state.json" "file_sha256" "2aaa69da7f902eacd1701b38c030cc87f3707a2961bdb9493a5cd1afb18e6c70"} {"question" "q-122633" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We notice the following:\n\n- The vertical component (i.e., the $j$ component) is zero for *every* vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nH(x,y)=y\\,i+j\n$$\n\n- As we move away from the origin in the vertical direction, our vectors' horizontal components (i.e., the $i$ components) get longer. Therefore, we can rule out the following options:\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=x\\,i,\\,K(x,y)=-i\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $G(x,y)=y\\,i.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/state.json" "file_sha256" "2aaa69da7f902eacd1701b38c030cc87f3707a2961bdb9493a5cd1afb18e6c70"} {"question" "q-122633" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5c3df36c5a5a48ba44e555bfdebc8a7077212df2cdc73b3578a5a527e6f046f7"} {"question" "q-122633" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/state.json" "file_sha256" "2aaa69da7f902eacd1701b38c030cc87f3707a2961bdb9493a5cd1afb18e6c70"} {"question" "q-122633" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "F(x,y)=x\\,i"] ["math" "G(x,y)=y\\,i"] ["math" "H(x,y)=y\\,i+j"] ["math" "K(x,y)=-i"] ["text" "None of the listed"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/state.json" "file_sha256" "2aaa69da7f902eacd1701b38c030cc87f3707a2961bdb9493a5cd1afb18e6c70"} {"question" "q-122633" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "G(x,y)=y\\,i"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/state.json" "file_sha256" "2aaa69da7f902eacd1701b38c030cc87f3707a2961bdb9493a5cd1afb18e6c70"} {"question" "q-122651" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/assets/7cb4dd61f9d42a48c022a183e7f4310a8a4ed7ae881edd136881ef6863282e2c.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/state.json" "file_sha256" "2aaa69da7f902eacd1701b38c030cc87f3707a2961bdb9493a5cd1afb18e6c70"} {"question" "q-122651" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We notice the following:\n\n- Each vector in our vector field is parallel to the $x$-axis. So, the $j$ and $k$ components of our vector field are zero everywhere. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=i+x\\,j\n$$\n\n- Moreover, each vector in our vector field is pointing in the *positive* $x$-direction, so the $i$ component of our vector field is positive. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nG(x,y,z)=-i\n$$\n\n- Finally, we note that each vector in our vector field has the same length, so the $i$ component of our vector field is constant. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nH(x,y,z)=x\\,i\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $K(x,y,z)=2\\,i.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/state.json" "file_sha256" "2aaa69da7f902eacd1701b38c030cc87f3707a2961bdb9493a5cd1afb18e6c70"} {"question" "q-122651" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5c3df36c5a5a48ba44e555bfdebc8a7077212df2cdc73b3578a5a527e6f046f7"} {"question" "q-122651" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/state.json" "file_sha256" "2aaa69da7f902eacd1701b38c030cc87f3707a2961bdb9493a5cd1afb18e6c70"} {"question" "q-122651" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "F(x,y,z)=i+x\\,j"] ["math" "G(x,y,z)=-i"] ["math" "H(x,y,z)=x\\,i"] ["math" "K(x,y,z)=2\\,i"] ["text" "None of the listed"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/state.json" "file_sha256" "2aaa69da7f902eacd1701b38c030cc87f3707a2961bdb9493a5cd1afb18e6c70"} {"question" "q-122651" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "K(x,y,z)=2\\,i"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/state.json" "file_sha256" "2aaa69da7f902eacd1701b38c030cc87f3707a2961bdb9493a5cd1afb18e6c70"} {"question" "q-122670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/assets/64f02fa7dcd23b20e61801c0453d8fe7ed013936572e1ee63f748361edd4dec5.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/state.json" "file_sha256" "2aaa69da7f902eacd1701b38c030cc87f3707a2961bdb9493a5cd1afb18e6c70"} {"question" "q-122670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We notice the following:\n\n- Each vector in our vector field is parallel to the $z$-axis. So, the $i$ and $j$ components of our vector field are zero everywhere. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=i,\\,G(x,y,z)=-j\n$$\n\n- Moreover, each vector in our vector field is pointing in the *negative* $z$-direction, so the $k$ component of our vector field is negative. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nH(x,y,z)=k\n$$\n\n- Finally, we note that each vector in our vector field has the same length, so the $k$ component of our vector field is constant. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nK(x,y,z)=-{x}^{2}\\,k\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram doesn't correspond to any of the listed vector fields." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/state.json" "file_sha256" "2aaa69da7f902eacd1701b38c030cc87f3707a2961bdb9493a5cd1afb18e6c70"} {"question" "q-122670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5c3df36c5a5a48ba44e555bfdebc8a7077212df2cdc73b3578a5a527e6f046f7"} {"question" "q-122670" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/state.json" "file_sha256" "2aaa69da7f902eacd1701b38c030cc87f3707a2961bdb9493a5cd1afb18e6c70"} {"question" "q-122670" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "F(x,y,z)=i"] ["math" "G(x,y,z)=-j"] ["math" "H(x,y,z)=k"] ["math" "K(x,y,z)=-{x}^{2}\\,k"] ["text" "None of the listed"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14067637/state.json" "file_sha256" "2aaa69da7f902eacd1701b38c030cc87f3707a2961bdb9493a5cd1afb18e6c70"} {"question" "q-122670" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "None of the listed"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake